   <standOff><listPerson><person xml:id="person3818"><persName type="main" xml:lang="bo-Latn-x-wylie">bya 'dul 'dzin brtson 'grus 'bar</persName><persName xml:lang="bo">བྱ་འདུལ་འཛིན་བརྩོན་འགྲུས་འབར</persName><persName type="alt" xml:lang="bo-Latn-x-wylie">bya 'dul 'dzin</persName><persName type="alt" xml:lang="bo-Latn-x-wylie">bya 'dul brtson 'grus 'bar</persName><persName type="alt" xml:lang="bo-Latn-x-wylie">bya 'du ba 'dzin ba brtson 'grus 'bar</persName><persName type="alt" xml:lang="bo-Latn-x-wylie">dge bshes zul phu ba</persName><persName type="alt" xml:lang="bo-Latn-x-wylie">sangs rgyas bya 'dul 'dzin brtson 'grus 'bar</persName><persName type="alt" xml:lang="bo-Latn-x-wylie">zul bya 'dul ba 'dzin pa</persName><persName type="alt" xml:lang="bo-Latn-x-wylie">zul phul bya 'dul ba 'dzin pa chen po</persName><birth notBefore="1091-01-01" notAfter="1100-12-31">after 1091 before 1100</birth><death notBefore="1147-01-01" notAfter="1174-12-31">after 1147 before 1174</death><sex value="M"/><nationality>Tibetan</nationality><idno type="BDRC">https://purl.bdrc.io/resource/P2273</idno><idno type="APIS">3818</idno><note type="comment">Born in 1091 at gTsang rong gyung and died at the age of 76 in Zul phu according to [R894SIKE]: 109.&#13;
[W4T5ZMUP]: 38 accordingly proposes the dates 1091-1166.&#13;
[VKBZTBWN], fol. 3b6 reports that he was born the year rNgog lo (ID:3786) came back to Tibet, i.e., ca. 1092.&#13;
On his life, based on the Zul phu mkhan byang chub rin chen dpal bzang po'i rnam par thar pa (ID:6715), see [W4T5ZMUP]: 40.&#13;
It is unclear whether he is the same person as rGya 'dul ba 'dzin pa (ID:4193). The [NA9AMDH6] distinguishes two "rGya 'dul 'dzin" - the elder (ID: 3941) and the younger (ID:4193) - and a "Bya 'dul 'dzin brTson 'grus 'bar" (student of 'Bre chen po). In contrast, the [R894SIKE] only mentions one "rGya 'dul 'dzin" (the elder), distinct from "Bya 'dul 'dzin" (who was ordained by 'Bre).&#13;
[VKBZTBWN], fol. 6b5-6 and [8VLVHDR2], fol. 14b5 report that he was ordained by 'Bre and received from him the name in religion brTson 'grus 'bar.&#13;
A number of the same teachers are mentioned for rGya 'dul 'dzin the younger and Bya 'dul 'dzin but, for instance, the latter's studies with rGya 'dul 'dzin the older took place when he was a retired abbot, whereas the former's studies with him took place when he was still abbot.&#13;
Further, rGya 'dul 'dzin the younger became abbot of dGa' ba sdong and Bya 'dul abbot of Zul phu.&#13;
This suggests they might have been distinct persons.</note></person><person xml:id="person3839"><persName type="main" xml:lang="bo-Latn-x-wylie">gtsang nag pa brtson 'grus seng ge</persName><persName xml:lang="bo">གཙང་ནག་པ་བརྩོན་འགྲུས་སེང་གེ</persName><persName type="alt" xml:lang="bo-Latn-x-wylie">brtson 'grus seng+ge</persName><persName type="alt" xml:lang="bo-Latn-x-wylie">gtsang nag pa</persName><persName type="alt" xml:lang="bo-Latn-x-wylie">gtsang nags brtson 'grus seng ge</persName><persName type="alt" xml:lang="bo-Latn-x-wylie">gtsang nags phug pa brtson 'grus seng ge</persName><persName type="alt" xml:lang="bo-Latn-x-wylie">brtson 'grus seng ge</persName><persName type="alt" xml:lang="bo-Latn-x-wylie">rtsang nag</persName><persName type="alt" xml:lang="bo-Latn-x-wylie">rtsang</persName><persName type="alt" xml:lang="bo-Latn-x-wylie">slob dpon gtsang nag pa</persName><persName type="alt" xml:lang="bo-Latn-x-wylie">mkhas pa rtsang nag pa</persName><persName type="alt" xml:lang="bo-Latn-x-wylie">dge slong brtson 'grus seng ge</persName><persName type="alt" xml:lang="bo-Latn-x-wylie">dge' slong brtson 'grus seng ge</persName><persName type="alt" xml:lang="bo-Latn-x-wylie">gtsang nags phug pa brtson 'grus seng ge</persName><persName type="alt" xml:lang="bo-Latn-x-wylie">dbu ma smra ba'i dge' slong bstson 'grus seng ge</persName><persName type="alt" xml:lang="bo-Latn-x-wylie">mang du thos pa'i dge slong brtson 'grus seng ge</persName><persName type="alt" xml:lang="bo-Latn-x-wylie">rigs par smra ba'i dge slong brtson 'grus seng ge</persName><persName type="alt" xml:lang="bo-Latn-x-wylie">shag kya'i dge slong brtson 'grus seng ge</persName><persName type="alt" xml:lang="bo-Latn-x-wylie">slob dpon grags pa'i dbang phyug gtsang nag pa</persName><persName type="alt" xml:lang="bo-Latn-x-wylie">vīryasiṃha</persName><birth notAfter="1150-12-31">before 1150</birth><death notBefore="1195-01-01">after 1195</death><sex value="M"/><nationality>Tibetan</nationality><idno type="BDRC">https://purl.bdrc.io/resource/P2259</idno><idno type="APIS">3839</idno><note type="comment">Van der Kuijp ([H9MPLMTV]) proposed the dates (?-1185). The terminus ante quem for gTsang nag pa's death was pushed to 1192 by Schwabland ([Q8WU9EDW]: 794, n. 3) on account of the date of Khro pu lo tsA ba (ID:3878)'s studies with gTsang nag pa. This date was corrected to 1195 based on Khro phu lo tsA ba's biography (van der Kuijp, personal communication).</note></person><person xml:id="person3880"><persName type="main" xml:lang="bo-Latn-x-wylie">gro ston bdud rtsi grags</persName><persName xml:lang="bo">གྲོ་སྟོན་བདུད་རྩི་གྲགས</persName><persName type="alt" xml:lang="bo-Latn-x-wylie">snar thang mkhan po a rmi ta kir ti</persName><persName type="alt" xml:lang="bo-Latn-x-wylie">gro mo che ba bdud rtsi grags</persName><persName type="alt" xml:lang="bo-Latn-x-wylie">gra ston chen po</persName><persName type="alt" xml:lang="bo-Latn-x-wylie">amṛtakīrti</persName><persName type="alt" xml:lang="bo-Latn-x-wylie">gro mo che</persName><birth notBefore="1153-01-01" notAfter="1153-12-31">1153</birth><death notBefore="1232-01-01" notAfter="1232-12-31">1232</death><sex value="M"/><nationality>Tibetan</nationality><idno type="BDRC">https://purl.bdrc.io/resource/P2271</idno><idno type="APIS">3880</idno><note type="comment">Fourth abbot of sNar thang (ID:4411). On his life see [NTGHCZA8]: 34-51.</note></person><person xml:id="person3884"><persName type="main" xml:lang="bo-Latn-x-wylie">'jam gsar ba shes rab 'od zer</persName><persName xml:lang="bo">འཇམ་གསར་བ་ཤེས་རབ་འོད་ཟེར</persName><persName type="alt" xml:lang="bo-Latn-x-wylie">'jam dbyangs gsar ma</persName><persName type="alt" xml:lang="bo-Latn-x-wylie">jo sras glo bde</persName><birth notBefore="1100-01-01" notAfter="1199-12-31">after 1100 before 1199</birth><death notBefore="1224-01-01" notAfter="1280-12-31">after 1224 before 1280</death><sex value="M"/><nationality>Tibetan</nationality><idno type="BDRC">https://purl.bdrc.io/resource/P2585</idno><idno type="APIS">3884</idno><note type="comment">Same person as gTsang nags phug pa 'jam dbyangs shes rab 'od zer (ID:6640)?&#13;
Late 13th-early 14th c. according to van der Kuijp ([H9MPLMTV]: 22). &#13;
Late 12th-early 13th c. according to [MX3PRVV2]: 3/16 and n. 4.&#13;
Considered to be identical with gNyal zhig's student 'Jam dbyangs gsar ma ([4LWBNM7B]: 121).&#13;
Important master in the Dro lineage of the Kālacakra ([MX3PRVV2]).&#13;
